        "id": "maxim:biology:physiology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physiology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Physiology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Example: Core temperature regulation\n  Set point: 37°C\n  Sensor: thermoreceptors (skin + hypothalamus)\n  Comparator: hypothalamus (thermostat)\n  Effectors: sweating (cool), shivering (warm), vasodilation/constriction"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#007",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:06-physiology, git-history:biology:06-physiology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
