      "text": "```\nPHYSIOLOGY ←→ CONTROL SYSTEMS AND DISTRIBUTED ARCHITECTURES"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:06-physiology, git-history:biology:06-physiology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[physiology]",
        "current_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:physiology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physiology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Physiology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Homeostasis = PID controller (mostly the I and P terms)\n  Proportional: response scales with deviation from set point (shiver harder if colder)\n  Integral: accumulated error drives long-term correction (RAAS for blood pressure)\n  Derivative: rate of change triggers preemptive response (feed-forward: exercise → HR\n    rises before O₂ drops)\n  Set point is not fixed: fever resets thermostat upward (hypothalamic response to IL-1β)\n  Cascaded loops: HPA axis is an outer loop modulating inner cortisol feedback loop"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:06-physiology, git-history:biology:06-physiology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[physiology]",
        "current_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:physiology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physiology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Physiology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Nervous system = low-latency event bus with specialized routing\n  Action potential: binary spike (all-or-nothing); frequency = signal intensity\n  Myelinated axons (Aα): 70-120 m/s — fast path for motor and proprioception\n  Unmyelinated C-fibers: 0.5-2 m/s — slow path for pain and temperature\n  Synapse: the routing node — can be excitatory (glutamate) or inhibitory (GABA)\n  Summation (spatial + temporal): logical OR/AND on incoming signals at the dendrite\n  CNS = hierarchical routing: spinal cord handles reflexes locally (low latency);\n    cortex handles complex decisions (high latency, high bandwidth)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#014",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:06-physiology, git-history:biology:06-physiology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[physiology]",
        "current_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:physiology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physiology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Physiology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Endocrine system = pub-sub with slow delivery and long TTL\n  Publisher: endocrine gland (pancreas, thyroid, adrenal)\n  Topic: hormone (insulin, T₃, cortisol) — travels in bloodstream = the message bus\n  Subscriber: any cell expressing the receptor — promiscuous fan-out\n  Latency: minutes to hours (vs ms for neural)\n  Duration: minutes to days (vs ms to seconds for neural)\n  Feedback: negative feedback loops close the loop (TSH → T₃ → inhibit TRH/TSH)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:06-physiology, git-history:biology:06-physiology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[physiology]",
        "current_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:physiology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physiology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Physiology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Immune system = adaptive intrusion detection system\n  Innate (pattern matching): fast, fixed signatures (PAMPs, TLR recognition)\n  Adaptive (signature learning): slow first response; generates custom antibodies\n  Memory: second exposure → pre-trained response, 100× faster, higher affinity\n  Self/non-self discrimination: central tolerance (thymic deletion) + peripheral tolerance\n  Failure modes:\n    Autoimmune = false positive (attacks self)\n    Immunodeficiency = false negative (misses pathogen)\n    Allergy = excessive response to harmless antigen\n  Affinity maturation = iterative ML: somatic hypermutation + antigen-selection rounds"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#016",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:biology:06-physiology, git-history:biology:06-physiology]",
        "canonical_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[physiology]",
        "current_path": "biology/06-PHYSIOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:biology:physiology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "biology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[physiology]",
        "section": "biology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Physiology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Cardiac output = queueing theory applied to a biological pump\n  CO = HR × SV (heart rate × stroke volume): throughput = rate × batch size\n  Starling's law: SV increases with preload (end-diastolic volume) — demand-responsive\n  Baroreflex: closed-loop control of MAP = CO × TPR — fast feedback (seconds)\n  RAAS: long-loop controller for chronic BP (minutes to hours)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#017",
      "path": [
        "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
