      "text": "ACTION POTENTIAL:\n  Resting: −70 mV (inside negative); maintained by Na⁺/K⁺ ATPase\n  Threshold: ~−55 mV\n  Rising phase: voltage-gated Na⁺ channels open → Na⁺ influx → depolarization\n  Peak: ~+40 mV; Na⁺ channels inactivate\n  Falling: K⁺ channels open → K⁺ efflux → repolarization\n  Undershoot: K⁺ channels slow to close → brief hyperpolarization\n  Absolute refractory period: no AP possible (Na⁺ channels inactivated)\n  Relative refractory: AP possible with stronger stimulus (K⁺ channels still open)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-PHYSIOLOGY.md#023",
